ate 1.5-mile hiking trail at Chip Ross Natural Area and identifies Lester Avenue parking access.","source_url":"https://www.corvallisoregon.gov/parksrec/page/chip-ross-park-and-natural-area","source_title":"Chip Ross Park and Natural Area | Corvallis Oregon","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Access is at the end of Lester Avenue; use designated trails and observe posted seasonal trail rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"peavy-arboretum-forest-discovery-trail","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Forest Discovery Trail at Peavy Arboretum","title":"Explore Peavy’s Forest Discovery Trail","subtitle":"Peavy Arboretum, 7 miles north of Corvallis","notes":"Pick up the self-guided materials and follow the 1.2-mile forest hike from Arboretum Parking, using the prompts to notice ecology and history.","short_summary":"A guided, hands-on forest walk at Peavy Arboretum.","evidence_claim":"OSU’s Forest Discovery Trail guide states that the program is free to use for OSU Research Forest visitors and takes place at Peavy Arboretum.","source_url":"https://cf.forestry.oregonstate.edu/sites/default/files/FDT_TeachersGuide.pdf","source_title":"Forest Discovery Trail Program Teacher’s Guide","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The trail begins from Arboretum Parking; plan for a 1.2-mile outdoor hike and check local conditions before leaving.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"corvallis-central-park","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Central Park","title":"Take a downtown Central Park break","subtitle":"650 NW Monroe Ave., Corvallis","notes":"Use the paved walkways, benches, playground, and sculpture stops for a relaxed downtown reset; leave dogs at home because they are not allowed here.","short_summary":"A downtown park with walkways, public art, benches, and a playground.","evidence_claim":"The City of Corvallis describes Central Park as a public downtown park with paved walkways, sculptures, resting benches, and a playground.","source_url":"https://www.corvallisoregon.gov/parksrec/page/central-park","source_title":"Central Park | Corvallis Oregon","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"City page lists the park at 650 NW Monroe Avenue and says dogs are not allowed.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
